<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Flinders Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Flinders Island is the largest island of the Furneaux Group in Bass Strait, north-east of Tasmania. From 1833 the surviving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aboriginal-tasmanians">Aboriginal Tasmanians</a>, gathered by George Augustus Robinson, were confined at the settlement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wybalenna">Wybalenna</a> on its west coast, where many died of disease. The remaining people were moved to Oyster Cove near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hobart">Hobart</a> in 1847.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/flinders-island.jpg" alt="Flinders Island" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flinders_island.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>During the Black War of the 1820s colonists and soldiers killed many Aboriginal Tasmanians, and the survivors were removed to Wybalenna on <b>Flinders Island</b> in the 1830s.</blockquote><a href="/state/colony-of-tasmania">Colony of Tasmania</a></li></ul></section>
